s(25, 'me-and-you', 'A strand of light from one side, a strand of flax from the staff on the other: they reach, miss, and join on "me and you".')
s(27, 'loom', 'The loom: the shuttle flies, the batten falls, and band by band the cloth of the generations grows.')
s(28, 'every-male', 'A row of wet clay rounds on a board; the seal comes down on each on the beat, and each mark lights and cools.')
s(29, 'curtain', 'The tent curtain falls closed before the lamplight: what is done within is not shown.')
s('126.5s', 'the-sign', 'A sealed round of clay hangs from above on the cord; on "sign" its mark lights.')
s(32, 'eight-days', 'Eight lamps in a row: seven small flames, and on "eight" the eighth takes, taller and brighter than them all.')
s(33, 'born-in-house', 'In the tent the staffs of the house stand in a row, old to young; a hung lamp swings, and their shadows sweep the curtain.')
s(34, 'strangers', 'A leather bag of silver is loosed on a striped cloth: the pieces run, roll, and settle by a stranger\'s blue-banded jar.')
s(36, 'one-flame', 'Lamps of the house in red clay and lamps of strangers in pale and blue, two lines meeting, lit from one fire.')
s(38, 'marked', 'Very close: the seal leaves the clay, and the mark stays, glowing in the dark earth as the camera goes round it.')
s(40, 'unmarked', 'The light passes along the row of rounds and each answers; one, blank, does not.')
